  "body": "Follow-up to #1315 (PR #1485), tested on macOS 27 (Apple silicon) with `/bin/bash` 3.2 and BSD sed at `0b4052bb`.\n\n**What happens:** after #1485, the script gets through the sysroot download, the `shasum` check and the `sed` patching on macOS. The link of `camcraft-cli` then fails with `rust-lld: error: … undefined symbol: ecs_has_id` (and `ecs_modified_id`, `ecs_cpp_set`, …). The `cc` crate archives the flecs C objects with Apple's `/usr/bin/ar` and `ranlib`, which only handle Mach-O. The flecs build warns `ranlib: warning: archive member 'flecs_rust.o' not a mach-o file`, and `libflecs.a` comes out at 96 bytes.\n\n**Confirmed fix:** with `AR_wasm32_unknown_unknown=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin/llvm-ar`, the archive is 2.1 MB, the script finishes, and `web/check-app-page.sh target/web` passes. `git status` stays clean.\n\n**Suggested change:** on macOS, when `AR_wasm32_unknown_unknown` isn't set, the script finds `llvm-ar` (on PATH, Homebrew's `$(brew --prefix llvm)/bin`, or rustup's `llvm-tools`) and exports it. With none found, it stops with a message naming what to install (`brew install llvm` or `rustup component add llvm-tools`) instead of failing at the link. \"Needs:\" in the header gains `llvm-ar` on macOS.\n\n**Done means:** #1315's own definition of done. `web/build-app-wasm.sh` and `web/check-app-page.sh` run unmodified on macOS with `/bin/bash` and BSD sed.\n",
